<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   600     vs 701</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    1,000   vs 911</p>
<p>    Group sales				  34,675  vs 32,094</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     Domestic				    14,986  vs 14,088</p>
<p>     International			     19,689  vs 18,006</p>
<p>Sales breakdown by business division:</p>
<p>     Engineering				 15,234  vs 13,870</p>
<p>     Automotive				   7,563  vs 7,200</p>
<p>     Telecommunications			 4,209  vs 2,716</p>
<p>     Tubes and trading			  6,647  vs 6,796</p>
<p>     Other companies			    1,528  vs 2,001</p>
<p>    Group orders received		    35,758  vs 34,900</p>
<p>Orders breakdown by business division:</p>
<p>     Engineering				 15,795  vs 16,190</p>
<p>     Automotive				   7,773  vs 7,331</p>
<p>     Telecommunications			 4,209  vs 2,716</p>
<p>     Tubes and trading			  6,802  vs 7,112</p>
<p>     Other companies			    1,242  vs 1,702</p>
<p>    Group investment			    3,420  vs 2,668</p>
<p>Investment breakdown by business division:</p>
<p>     Engineering				    786  vs 877</p>
<p>     Automotive				     393  vs 389</p>
<p>     Telecommunications			 1,932  vs 938</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>	Mannesmann Mobilfunk			753  vs 857</p>
<p>	Arcor					 1,045  vs n/a</p>
<p>	Eurokom					 134  vs 81</p>
<p>     Tubes and trading			    214  vs 237</p>
<p>     Other companies				 95  vs 227</p>
<p>    Group workforce on Dec 31		119,675 vs 122,684</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     Domestic				     78,015 vs 81,004</p>
<p>     International				41,660 vs 41,680</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German engineering company is Mannesmann AG. The investment figure for Arcor represents the purchase price Mannesmann as part of a consortium which last year acquired 49.8 percent of DBKom GmbH, the telecommunications unit of railway Deutsche Bahn AG. Mannesmann holds 60 percent of the consortium, which includes AT&amp;T Corp, Deutsche Bank and the European Unisource group.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
